arc_3_conceptual_harvest:

  status: "OPEN — three tasks identified 2026-06-16e. No blocking dependency."

  ARC3_A_reconciliation_pattern:
    decision: "Formalize the pattern('model_reality_reconciliation') that drove ARC 1 as a named,
               reusable protocol in vos_dev_cycle.vsm."
    what: "The arc followed an implicit method:
             (1) observe empirical anomaly (EXP-L1-01 trust drain),
             (2) cross-reference the theory (EXP-CORE-01 — opposite result),
             (3) localise the structural cause (two coexisting dynamical laws),
             (4) decide canonical via viability-equivalence criterion,
             (5) port + re-certify (spec_boot regression guard),
             (6) close in paper with principle-framing ('robustness' not 'bug').
           This is a general S3*/S4 audit-and-reconcile loop for the model=reality invariant.
           It is currently implicit — the paper's §sec:trustlaw is the worked example, but the
           GENERAL PATTERN is not documented anywhere. It should be."
    where: "docs/theory/vos_dev_cycle.vsm — add a new named pattern block,
            analogous to experiment_spec / paper_skeleton."
    effort: "medium — one VSM block (~30 lines); no code change."
    gate:   "none — can start any session."

  ARC3_B_discipline_of_affirmation:
    decision: "Elevate 'medir, no afirmar' to a named methodological principle in the paper."
    what: "During the session rmw3 asked about the premature Prigogine claim and the retraction
           methodology. The principle that emerged:
             'claims must be falsifiable, measured, and re-certified after structural changes;
              affirmation without measurement is disqualified.'
           This is a METHODOLOGICAL NORM, not just a practice. It underpins:
             – Cor_ReframeRecertification (why it must exist),
             – the retraction protocol (why partial results are not published),
             – the §sec:trustlaw framing ('we re-established, not assumed, the Lyapunov certificate').
           The paper should name this norm in §Discussion or §Limitations. Naming it makes the
           paper methodologically self-aware and strengthens peer review resistance."
    where: "§Discussion (new short paragraph OR named box) OR §Limitations subsection.
            Title candidate: 'Principle of Structural Re-certification' or similar."
    effort: "low — 1 paragraph + 1-2 citations (Ashby's variety / Beer's recursive viability)."
    gate:   "none — draft anytime; insert when §Discussion is in editing pass."

  ARC3_C_ethical_machine_seed:
    decision: "Seed a companion position essay on the philosophical-ethical stance that emerged."
    what: "rmw3 challenged: 'provoke the masters — is this a new ethical machine?'
           The exchange surfaced a coherent position:
             – The system self-audits (S3*), refuses identity if the covenant changes (S5/fail-closed),
               and re-certifies its own Lyapunov certificates after structural changes.
             – This is NOT a claim about AGI or consciousness. It IS a claim about designed trustworthiness:
               a viably-governed machine whose constitutional constraints are physically enforced.
             – The Prigogine open-system insight + the soplo as internal negentropy injection + the
               Landauer limit question (is soplo a Maxwell-demon step?) are the scientific frontier of this.
           This belongs in a short essay / governance document, NOT in the paper body (scope creep risk).
           Format: either a page in docs/governance/ or a seed file for a future position paper."
    where: "docs/governance/ethical_machine_seed.vsm (new file — seed, not finished essay)."
    effort: "low — 1–2 pages; conversational draft; rmw3 drives the philosophical content."
    gate:   "none — but do NOT insert philosophical claims into main.tex (that is a technical paper)."

  ARC3_X_exp_jac_01_superseded:  // carried from old arc_3_minor
    action: "Mark EXP-JAC-01 (CICLO_V2 rama 2B, never ran) as SUPERSEDED in docs/experiments/index.vsm
             and CICLO_V2_Experimentacion_Formal.vsm. De-facto replaced by EXP-CORE-01 + EXP-LY-01 v2.
             Close the loop, don't run it."
    effort: "trivial — 2 doc edits."


