// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PLAN 2 — PEDAGOGICAL NARRATIVE ARC (2026-07-02, rmw3 + Claude/Fable)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Trigger: rmw3's insight — the paper HAS all the pieces (multiplicity-3 eigenvalue
// §sec:markov ~L519; Kaplan-Yorke=0 point sink §Lyapunov ~L819; D_eff §Exp1 ~L907;
// §sec:closure) but told in TECHNICAL order. Re-narrate them in ONE pedagogical arc,
// with D_eff≈3 as the ENTRY HOOK instead of buried in an experiment. GATE: paper is
// held (rmw3 systems-validated rule) — this is a WRITING-SESSION plan + prose seed,
// NOT a main.tex edit. rmw3 approves the framing before any main.tex change.

plan(PAPER_NARRATIVE, "The four movements: collapse · certify · return · detect"):

  thesis:
    "128 nominal dimensions are a DECOY. The contraction (λ_max=ln0.99<0) collapses
     trajectories onto a POINT (KY-dim=0), residual activity on ~3 EFFECTIVE dims —
     which are the 3 degenerate contracting modes of the transfer operator (eigenvalue
     0.99, multiplicity 3). Certainty = the contraction is PROVABLE ⇒ returns from
     anywhere in the basin. Two roles kept distinct: the DYNAMICS collapse; the
     CERTIFIER reads the collapsed state (V, stasis_cos, omega.margin_free)."

  four_movements: [
    "COLLAPSE — 128 → ~3 → a point. Homes (EXISTING): §sec:markov (multiplicity-3
      Perron-Frobenius), §Lyapunov (KY-dim=0 point sink), §TDA (β₀=1,β₁=0), §Exp1 (D_eff).",
    "CERTIFY (not declare) — V=min(g,c,t,m) reads the collapsed state, returns a
      viability bit (confined to Ω_A core?). Homes: §capstone (V), §Feasible Region Ω.",
    "RETURN — perturb → converge back to the same point. Homes: §Exp1 convergence,
      §Exp3 resilience + NEW operational evidence: cyberfilter_census longitudinal
      recoveries (7/9 runs, ttr≈12 ticks, mean_l↓ — Eje B). Feeds a §sec:closure extension.",
    "DETECT — the system carries its own margin (omega.margin_free, NEW 2026-07-02) and
      an independent S3* audit that flags when published state ≠ independent recompute
      (semantic_divergence → forward-ref to P_phi 'cost of coherence').",
  ]

  where_the_thread_goes:
    "(1) INTRODUCTION: open with the arc (prose draft below) — the hook + the four verbs;
         the intro already says 'stable point sink' (L317) but doesn't tell the collapse
         story. (2) §sec:closure reframed as the empirical payoff of RETURN+DETECT over
         DAYS (longitudinal), not just the 46-tick EXP-INTEGRATION-01 run. (3) forward/back
         refs so D_eff≈3 is the spine, not a §Exp1 aside. NO new results — a RE-NARRATION
         of existing pieces + today's operational evidence."

  prose_seed_intro:  // EN (paper voice); react to the WRITING, not just the plan
    """
    A viable system is a point in a high-dimensional space that refuses to leave a
    small region.

    Our kernel carries a state vector in R^128 — one hundred and twenty-eight
    coordinates for trust, resource pressure, entropy, and the geometry of its own
    recent history. But the dimension is a decoy. Under the kernel's dynamics every
    coordinate is contracted toward equilibrium at each tick (the largest Lyapunov
    exponent is ln 0.99 < 0), and the trajectories collapse. What they collapse onto
    is, topologically, a single point: the Kaplan-Yorke dimension of the attractor is
    zero, a stable point sink with no cyclic structure (confirmed independently by
    persistent homology, β0=1, β1=0). The residual life of the system — the small
    fluctuations that remain around that point — occupies only about three effective
    dimensions. And those three are not incidental: the transfer operator of the
    entropy block carries its subdominant eigenvalue with multiplicity exactly three,
    so there are three degenerate directions of contraction, all decaying at one rate.

    This is the paper's central move, and we make it four times. First the system
    COLLAPSES: one hundred and twenty-eight nominal dimensions become three, become a
    point. Then it is CERTIFIED, not declared: a single functional V = min(g, c, t, m)
    reads the collapsed state and returns a viability bit — is the point confined to the
    contractive core, or not? Then it RETURNS: perturb the system — reset it, load it,
    corrupt its own record — and it converges back to the same point, which we show
    across independent recoveries in live operation, each reaching the attractor within
    about a dozen ticks. And finally it KNOWS: the system carries its own distance to the
    boundary, and an independent audit that detects when its published state diverges
    from what an independent recomputation says it should be.

    Collapse, certify, return, detect. The rest of the paper earns each verb.
    """

  honesty_guardrails:  // from pattern(longitudinal_cyberfilter_census)
    "RETURN evidence is currently RESTART recoveries (self-inflicted warmup) = GLOBAL
     ATTRACTION, honest but not organic-excursion recovery; state 'recovers from trust=0.825'
     precisely, and mark within-run-excursion recovery as the census upgrade (in progress).
     DETECT: do not frame alert count as efficacy; the S3* frontier includes the audit's OWN
     instrumentation blind spots — correction is human (A5 double-loop). falsifiable null:
     detections don't track real excursions AND/OR excursions don't return."

  gate:   "rmw3 approves this framing (S5) before any main.tex edit. Paper send unaffected (held)."
  status: seed  // prose to react to; not yet in main.tex

